---
/**
 * ProofRule — the central claim of the quality-engineering material, drawn.
 *
 * Two runs of the same suite: one with the defect catalogue off, one with a
 * single defect switched on. The left panel is what a green suite actually
 * tells you (nothing); the right is detection, with the failure naming itself.
 */
---

<figure class="lu-figure proof-rule">
  <div class="lu-figure__frame">
    <div class="panels">
      <section class="panel">
        <p class="flag">all flags off</p>
        <ul class="tests">
          <li class="pass"><span class="mark">✓</span>checkout completes</li>
          <li class="pass"><span class="mark">✓</span>discount applied</li>
          <li class="pass"><span class="mark">✓</span>stock decremented</li>
          <li class="pass"><span class="mark">✓</span>order confirmed</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="message message--none">no failure to read</p>
        <p class="verdict">
          <span class="verdict__label">What you know</span>
          <span class="verdict__value">Nothing.</span>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="panel panel--proof">
        <p class="flag flag--on">TRAIL-DISCOUNT-ROUNDING on</p>
        <ul class="tests">
          <li class="pass"><span class="mark">✓</span>checkout completes</li>
          <li class="fail"><span class="mark">✗</span>discount applied</li>
          <li class="pass"><span class="mark">✓</span>stock decremented</li>
          <li class="pass"><span class="mark">✓</span>order confirmed</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="message">order total was <b>48.59</b>, expected <b>48.60</b></p>
        <p class="verdict">
          <span class="verdict__label">What you know</span>
          <span class="verdict__value verdict__value--proof">This suite catches that bug, and names it.</span>
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="lu-figure__caption">
    A suite is proven by the defects it catches, not by passing. Every acceptance
    test in this material is stated as the right-hand panel.
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .panels {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .panel {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding: 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline);
    border-radius: var(--lu-radius-control);
    background: var(--lu-surface-2);
  }

  .panel--proof {
    border-color: var(--sl-color-gray-5);
  }

  .flag {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
  }

  .flag--on {
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
  }

  .tests {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.375rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }

  .tests li {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    align-items: baseline;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
  }

  .mark {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 0.9em;
    font-weight: 590;
  }

  .pass .mark {
    color: var(--sl-color-green-high);
  }

  .fail {
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-1);
  }

  .fail .mark {
    color: var(--sl-color-red-high);
  }

  .message {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0.5rem 0.625rem;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--sl-color-red-high);
    background: var(--sl-color-red-low);
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
  }

  .message--none {
    border-left-color: var(--sl-color-gray-5);
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-4);
  }

  .verdict {
    margin-top: auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.25rem;
    margin: 0;
    padding-top: 0.75rem;
    border-top: 1px dashed var(--sl-color-gray-5);
  }

  .verdict__label {
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-4);
  }

  .verdict__value {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 510;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
  }

  .verdict__value--proof {
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }

  @media (max-width: 44rem) {
    .panels {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
